e":"SERIES","url":"","style":{"image":"https://cloud01.albox.co/shows/580b1ae0-1358-43de-acb0-38382c366334.jpg"},"length":0,"continue_watching_progress":0},{"items":[],"id":37169,"title":"The Fragrant Flower Blooms with Dignity","description":"","card_type":"normalPoster","type":"SERIES","url":"","style":{"image":"https://cloud02.albox.co/shows/447d7f23-84fc-42a4-9408-4ddc6677e158.jpg"},"length":0,"continue_watching_progress":0},{"items":[],"id":20993,"title":"Bleach","description":"","card_type":"normalPoster","type":"SERIES","url":"","style":{"image":"https://cdn6.albox.co/storage/disk51/shows/1805ad59-b8ad-40b5-a413-70904bf2afc7.jpg"},"length":0,"continue_watching_progress":0}],"id":0,"title":"Related","section_type":"normalPoster"},{"data":[{"items":[],"id":19102,"title":"","description":"3","card_type":"comments","type":"comments","url":"","style":null,"length":0,"continue_watching_progress":0}],"id":0,"title":"Comments","section_type":"comments"}],"post_info":{"genres":["Action","Sci-Fi","Crime","War","Seinen","Mecha"],"id":19102,"type":"SERIES","title":"Ghost in the Shell: Stand Alone Complex","logo":"","image":"https://cdn6.albox.co/storage/disk43/seasons/3eea377b-f8b1-4a25-bd66-6bade5b2f257.jpg","background_image":"https://cdn6.albox.co/storage/disk58/seasons/7b15b18e-7bb7-4319-9a11-611f9f4d8e15.jpg","likes":66,"dislikes":2,"views":5604,"release_date":"1099785600000","season_number":1,"description":"The second season of Ghost in The Shell: Stand Alone Complex begins with Section 9 being called back to work after a hostage situation of concern to the Ruling Party renders the Police useless. The entire team returns to the front lines: Kusanagi, Batoh, Togusa, Ishikawa, Saito, Paz & Borma, with four of the original Tachikomas restored after the firefight of Episode 26. The hostage situation announced the rising of a new terrorist cell, which takes much after another one in the headlines of today's papers. The Individual Eleven, whose members are neither individuals, or total up to eleven are a new threat to Public Security. How does a specialized public security group face an enemy more faceless than the \"laughing man\" during a time of political unrest? Among the broad changes from the first show involve the new ruling party, headed by the new Prime Minister Kabayuki after the prior ousting in GITS: SAC, the Japanese Residents caught in the middle of the affairs and paying the taxes for jobs they're going to lose in a time of recession, and the downtrodden \"invited\" Asian Immigrants of the Second Vietnamese War who were brought to Japan as a half-hearted humanitarian act from the government who was really just seeking cheap labor. And just who is the man called \"Gohda\", a mysterious new 'supervisor' (don't worry, Aramaki still runs the group) who appears to be calling the shots for Section 9 during certain missions? He calls out orders as if he was in charge of the group, yet has no apparent loyalty or respect to the government, military or Section 9.","rating":{"sources":[{"title":"IMDb","logo":"https://a7.pnghunt.com/preview/450/662/555/computer-wallpaper-text-brand-yellow-imdb.jpg","max_value":10,"value":8.5}],"value":8.5,"age":"r"},"current_season_id":7594,"content_control":"NORMAL"}}